And Peter came up to Jesus and said to Him, “Lord, how often shall I forgive my brother when he sins against me? Up to seven times?” Luke
And Jesus said to him, “Not just seven times, but seventy times seven.”
With that said, the Kingdom of Heaven is like a king who wants to settle accounts with his servants,
And as he began to settle accounts with them, they brought him someone who owed millions of dirhams in silver.
And since he had nothing to repay with, he ordered his master to sell him, his wife, and his children, and everything he possessed, in order to repay his debt.
And the slave prostrated to Him and said: Be patient, my master, and I will return everything that is due to you.
And his master had mercy on him and divorced him and allowed him to settle his debt.
And when that slave went out, he found one of the slaves with his companion who was asking him a hundred dirhams of silver, so he grabbed him and hanged him and said: Return to me what I was asking you for!
And his companion fell at his feet, begging him, and said to him: Be patient, and I will return to you what is yours.
But he refused, and they took him and threw him in jail until he pays off his debt.
And the people saw the slaves and their companions what had happened, they were very saddened and went to inform their master of all that had occurred.
And his master was yelling at him and said: Oh, this slave who isn't good! I forgave you all that debt because you made me desire [it].
Eva, why didn't you have mercy on your servant as I had mercy on you?
And his master worries, and sends him to prison to be tortured until he returns what he owes.
The path ahead will do for you what’s in the heavens, unless each of you truly forgives his brother from the bottom of his heart.
Chapter Nineteen: Jesus Teaches About Divorce
And when Jesus had finished these sayings, he departed from Galilee and went into Judea beyond the Jordan.
And many groups of people followed him and healed them.
And the Pharisees drew near to Him and tested Him, asking, “Is it lawful for a man to divorce his wife for any reason?”
And he answered them and said: “Didn’t you read in the Book of God that God created man from clay, male and female?”
And he said: This is why a man will leave his father and mother and unite with his wife, and they will become one.
And so you won't be two, but become one. And what God brings together, no man can tear apart.
And the Pharisees came to Him and asked, “Why did Moses command to give a certificate of divorce to a woman and to dismiss her?” Matthew
And Jesus answered them, “Because of your hard hearts, Moses allowed you to divorce your wives, but from the beginning it was not so, when God created Adam and Eve.”
I tell you that whoever divorces his wife for any reason except sexual immorality, and marries another, commits adultery.” Matthew 5:32; 1 Corinthians 7:10, 11
And he said to his students: “If this is the case between a man and a woman, it’s better for him not to marry at all.”
And Jesus answered them, “Not everyone accepts this word, only those whom God has enabled to accept it.”
There are people who are born from their mothers' wombs unable to marry, and there are those whom people have made that way. And there are those who do not marry for the sake of the Kingdom of Heaven. Whoever is able to understand this, let him understand.” Jesus blessed the little children.
And people brought him some small children so he could lay his hands on them and pray for them, and the disciples rebuked those who brought them.
But Jesus said, “Let the little children come to me, and do not hinder them, for the kingdom of heaven belongs to such as these.”
He put his hands on them and walked away from there. The young man who is dressed like that.
And a young man came to him and said, “O teacher, what good deed can I do to have eternal life?”
And Jesus answered him, “Why do you ask me about what is good? God alone is good. If you want to enter life, keep the commandments.”
And he was asking him: “What commandments?” And Jesus answered him: “Do not kill, do not commit adultery, do not steal, do not bear false witness,
Be kind to your father and mother, and want for others what you want for yourself.
And he was saying to the young man: “I’ve followed all these instructions, so what else do I need to do?”
And Jesus answered him, “If you want to be perfect, go sell all that you have and give to the poor, and you will have treasure in heaven, and come, follow me.”
But as soon as Milly heard these words from the young man, she left, feeling sad because things were already very difficult for her.
